<div class="container">
    <div class="text-center">
        <h1 class="display-5">Cookie Policy</h1>
    </div>
    <p>Last updated: March 30, 2026</p>
    <p>This Cookie Policy explains what Cookies &amp; the similar technology of Session Storage are and how I use them. You should read this policy so You can understand what client-side data storage I use, or the information I collect and how that information is used. This Cookie Policy has been created with the help of the <a href="https://www.termsfeed.com/cookies-policy-generator/" target="_blank">TermsFeed Cookies Policy Generator</a>.</p>
    <p>Cookies and Session Storage do not typically contain any information that personally identifies a user, but personal information that I may store about You may be linked to the information stored in and obtained from either technology.</p>
    <p>I do not store sensitive personal information such as names in the data storage I use.</p>
    <hr />
    <h2>Interpretation and Definitions</h2>
    <h3>Interpretation</h3>
    <p>The words whose initial letters are capitalized have meanings defined under the following conditions. The following definitions shall have the same meaning regardless of whether they appear in singular or in plural.</p>
    <br />
    <h3>Definitions</h3>
    <p>For the purposes of this Cookie Policy:</p>
    <ul class="container">
        <li><strong>App</strong> (referred to as either &quot;the App&quot;, &quot;the Web App&quot;, &quot;I&quot;, &quot;Me&quot; or &quot;My&quot; in this Cookie Policy) refers to Blackjack Web App, accessible from <a href="https://github.com/jaydenmuzzin/blackjack-web-app/blob/main/Blackjack/bin/Release/net9.0/Blackjack.exe" rel="external nofollow noopener" target="_blank">https://github.com/jaydenmuzzin/blackjack-web-app/blob/main/Blackjack/bin/Release/net9.0/Blackjack.exe</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Cookies</strong> means small files that are placed on Your computer, mobile device or any other device by a website or web application, containing details of your browsing history on that website or web application among its many uses.</li>
        <li><strong>Session Storage</strong> is a component of the Web Storage API enabling websites and web applications to store temporary, client-side data within a user's browser that only persists for as long as the tab or window session remains open.</li>
        <li><strong>You</strong> means the individual accessing or using the Web App, or a company, or any legal entity on behalf of which such individual is accessing or using the Web App, as applicable.</li>
    </ul>
    <hr />
    <h2>The use of Client-Side Data Storage</h2>
    <h3>Types of Cookies I Use</h3>
    <p>Cookies can be &quot;Persistent&quot; or &quot;Session&quot; Cookies. Persistent Cookies remain on your personal computer or mobile device when You go offline, while Session Cookies are deleted as soon as You close your web browser.</p>
    <p>Where required by law, I will request your consent before using Cookies that are not strictly necessary.</p>
    <p>I do not use either the Persistent or Session type of Cookies in the Web App.</p>
    <br />
    <h3>Session Storage I Use</h3>
    <p>Session Storage and its items differs from Session Cookies. Unlike Session Cookies, Session Storage items are:</p>
    <p>
        <ul class="container">
            <li>Restricted to a single tab, not shared across multiple tabs &amp; windows of the same browser instance</li>
            <li>Cleared when the tab is closed, not only when all browser windows are closed</li>
            <li>Only stored in the browser, not potentially on the server</li>
            <li>Not automatically sent to the server with every HTTP request</li>
        </ul>
    </p>
    <p>Session Storage is used to provide the Web App and cannot be switched off in My systems.</p>
    <p>I use Session Storage for the purpose set out below:</p>
    <ul class="container">
        <li>
            <p><strong>Functional</strong></p>
            <p>Administered by: Me</p>
            <p>Purpose: This data enables services available through the Web App and allows the App to remember choices You make when You use the Web App, such as your username &amp; player settings, to provide a more personalised experience. This data authenticates users and prevents fraudulent player activity. More specifically, this data allows You to reconnect to a game You disconnected from in the state the game is currently in, simultaneously restoring the previously saved settings prior to disconnection, and thus avoiding requiring You to re-enter your settings every time You are reconnected to the game. I only use this data placed in Session Storage to provide You with these services.</p>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <hr />
    <h2>Consent</h2>
    <h3>Your Choices Regarding Cookies</h3>
    <p>If You prefer to avoid the use of Cookies on the Web App, first You must disable the use of Cookies in your browser and then delete the Cookies saved in your browser associated with the Web App. You may use this option for preventing the use of Cookies at any time.</p>
    <p>If You do not accept My Cookies, You may experience some inconvenience in your use of the Web App and some features may not function properly.</p>
    <h4>Deleting Cookies</h4>
    <p>If You'd like to delete Cookies or instruct your web browser to delete or refuse Cookies, please visit the help pages of your web browser.</p>
    <ul class="container">
        <li>
            <p>For the Chrome web browser, please visit this page from Google: <a href="https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/32050" rel="external nofollow noopener" target="_blank">https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/32050</a></p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>For the Edge web browser, please visit this page from Microsoft: <a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/manage-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-view-allow-block-delete-and-use-168dab11-0753-043d-7c16-ede5947fc64d" rel="external nofollow noopener" target="_blank">https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/manage-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-view-allow-block-delete-and-use-168dab11-0753-043d-7c16-ede5947fc64d</a></p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>For the Firefox web browser, please visit this page from Mozilla: <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-Me/kb/delete-cookies-remove-info-websites-stored" rel="external nofollow noopener" target="_blank">https://support.mozilla.org/en-Me/kb/delete-cookies-remove-info-websites-stored</a></p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>For the Safari web browser, please visit this page from Apple: <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/guide/safari/sfri11471/mac" rel="external nofollow noopener" target="_blank">https://support.apple.com/en-au/guide/safari/sfri11471/mac</a></p>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>For any other web browser, please visit your web browser's official web pages.</p>
    <br />
    <h3>Your Choices Regarding Session Storage</h3>
    <p>If You prefer to avoid the use of Session Storage on the Web App, first You must disable the use of Session Storage in your browser and then delete the Session Storage items saved in your browser associated with the Web App. You may use this option for preventing the use of Session Storage at any time.</p>
    <p>If You do not accept My Session Storage, You may experience some inconvenience in your use of the Web App and some features may not function properly.</p>
    <h4>Disabling Session Storage</h4>
    <p>Browsers typically do not allow disabling Session Storage separately from disabling the use of cookies and/or site data.</p>
    <p>To disable Session Storage in the Firefox web browser, follow the instructions below:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Type "about:config" into the address bar and press 'Enter' to view your internal browser settings. If required, press the "Accept the Risk and Continue" button.</li>
        <li>In the 'Search preference name' search bar, type "dom.storage.enabled".</li>
        <li>Press the toggle button on the right side of the result, which will set the value to "false", thereby disabling both local &amp; session DOM Storage.</li>
    </ol>
    <br />
    <h4>Deleting Session Storage Items</h4>
    <p>If You'd like to delete Session Storage or instruct your web browser to delete or refuse Session Storage, please visit the help pages of your web browser.</p>
    <ul class="container">
        <li>
            <p>For the Chrome web browser, please visit this page from Google: <a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/14114868" rel="external nofollow noopener" target="_blank">https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/14114868</a></p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>For the Edge web browser, please visit this page from Microsoft: <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/devtools/storage/sessionstorage#delete-sessionstorage-key-value-pairs" rel="external nofollow noopener" target="_blank">https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/devtools/storage/sessionstorage#delete-sessionstorage-key-value-pairs</a></p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>For the Firefox web browser, please visit this page from Mozilla: <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/storage" rel="external nofollow noopener" target="_blank">https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/storage</a></p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>For the Safari web browser, follow the instructions below:</p>
            <p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Click "Safari", then "Preferences...".</li>
                    <li>In the 'Preferences' dialog, select the "Advanced" tab.</li>
                    <li>At the bottom of the dialog, check the "Show Develop menu in menu bar" preference.</li>
                    <li>Close the 'Preferences' dialog.</li>
                    <li>Click "Develop", then "Show Web Inspector".</li>
                    <li>In the Web Inspector, select the "Console" tab.</li>
                    <li>Either type <code>&nbsp;sessionStorage.clear();&nbsp;</code> in the field and press 'Enter' to clear all items, or type <code>&nbsp;sessionStorage.removeItem("&lt;item name&gt;");&nbsp;</code>, where <code>&lt;item name&gt;</code> is the name of a session storage item, and press 'Enter' to delete a single item.</li>
                    <li>Close the Web Inspector and refresh the page.</li>
                </ol>
            </p>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>For any other web browser, please visit your web browser's official web pages.</p>
